{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f2d718b5-8107-4cd0-b67b-a61d6511f445","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89f6b9b6bd7a2754","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-_m4vwrya/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Administrator GPU chargeback reporting views in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the administrator-facing reporting views in the RHOAI Dashboard: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, rendered from the stable chargeback reporting API, and a current-month view showing each project's consumption against its Kueue quota. This is the user-facing half of the chargeback reporting capability. All consumption data is retrieved through the stable reporting API; Kueue quota data is read through the Dashboard's existing Kubernetes CR-based integration model.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Administrator report view: per-project GPU-hour consumption over selectable time ranges, consuming the stable reporting API.\n- Current-month chargeback view: each project's current-month GPU-hour consumption shown against its Kueue quota, with the quota side read from Kueue CRs (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) per the Dashboard's existing integration conventions.\n- Administrator-scoped access to the new views, following the Dashboard's existing RBAC/project-scoping conventions.\n- Enablement of the new views through the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag/config conventions.\n- Incidental navigation and caption updates needed to surface the views (no standalone content authoring).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the stable reporting API returns per-project GPU-hour data, the administrator view displays consumption per project for any selected time range.\n- The current-month view shows, per project, both current-month GPU-hour consumption (from the reporting API) and the project