{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f85c78056208183","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Administrator GPU chargeback reporting views in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Administrator GPU chargeback reporting views in the Dashboard\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tDelivers the administrator-facing reporting views in the RHOAI Dashboard: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, rendered from the stable chargeback reporting API, and a current-month view showing each project's consumption against its Kueue quota. This is the user-facing half of the chargeback reporting capability. All consumption data is retrieved through the stable reporting API; Kueue quota data is read through the Dashboard's existing Kubernetes CR-based integration model.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Administrator report view: per-project GPU-hour consumption over selectable time ranges, consuming the stable reporting API.\n39\t- Current-month chargeback view: each project's current-month GPU-hour consumption shown against its Kueue quota, with the quota side read from Kueue CRs (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) per the Dashboard's existing integration conventions.\n40\t- Administrator-scoped access to the new views, following the Dashboard's existing RBAC/project-scoping conventions.\n41\t- Enablement of the new views through the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag/config conventions.\n42\t- Incidental navigation and caption updates needed to surface the views (no standalone content authoring).\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given the stable reporting API returns per-project GPU-hour data, the administrator view displays consumption per project for any selected time range.\n47\t- The current-month view shows, per project, both current-month GPU-hour consumption (from the reporting API) and the project's Kueue quota, with the comparison rendered against both values, and the quota semantics match the Distributed Workloads ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model.\n48\t- The views are accessible only to users in the administrator scope, consistent with the Dashboard's existing RBAC model.\n49\t- The views can be enabled and disabled through the Dashboard's existing feature-flag/config mechanism.\n50\t- The views render correctly against representative report data, verified by automated UI tests or equivalent verification.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-1 (P0): administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges — the view surface over the reporting API.\n55\t- HLR-3 (P1): the Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota — bundled with the P0 report view because it renders the same consumption data in the same administrator view surface and reuses its project scoping; it is not separately schedulable.\n56\t\n57\t## Risks / Notes\n58\t\n59\t- Depends on the stable per-project GPU-hour reporting API (over selectable time ranges) being available as a build-against contract; the Dashboard work is shielded from metering-schema drift by that API and proceeds in parallel with the metering integration work.\n60\t- Kueue quota semantics (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) must be interpreted consistently with the Distributed Workloads quota model.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f7af457fe3af600","agent_id":"adbb64701485d60d1","session_id":"9bcc61a9-70a5-417c-9026-158475c20fef","uuid":"0a8c08ee-b4da-4251-a11b-100694b43cff","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:53:05.657Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f85c78056208183","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
