 discrepancies found between draft-contract assumptions and the final schema, including test fixture updates.\n41\t- Confirmation of the report-semantics definition (what counts as a GPU-hour) against the metering strategy's semantics, recorded as the authoritative input to the documentation.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The report computation and API consume the finalized metering data schema, with all draft-contract assumptions either confirmed or replaced by the final schema — no draft-only field mappings remain.\n46\t- End-to-end validation on real metering output: computed per-project GPU-hour totals for sample projects and time ranges match the metering source data within a documented, justified tolerance (exact where exactness is expected).\n47\t- The authoritative report-semantics definition (GPU-hour counting, time-range boundaries, per-project attribution) is confirmed against the metering strategy's semantics and recorded as the handoff input to the documentation work.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990 — completes real-data delivery and validation of the reporting capability.\n52\t\n53\t## Risks / Notes\n54\t\n55\t- Externally controlled precondition: this epic's integration work completes only against the finalized metering data schema, which lands when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. That timing is outside this strategy's control and cannot be compressed by this epic. The Tier-1 build (report backend and Dashboard views against the draft contract) proceeds in parallel and is not blocked by this precondition.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f7af457fe3af600","agent_id":"adbb64701485d60d1","session_id":"9bcc61a9-70a5-417c-9026-158475c20fef","uuid":"d76eebc8-63fc-4525-b74f-c7693abac514","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:53:06.274Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d4b9e10bb3525df","permission_decision":{"decisio