k-product type mixing — E002 explicitly excludes standalone content\n62\tauthoring, which is carried by E004. No epic appears to exceed ~2 weeks; no re-split\n63\ttriggers needed.\n64\t\n65\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n66\tAll four epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (report backend +\n67\tAPI + CSV, Dashboard views, reconciled/validated integration, published documentation).\n68\tE004 correctly carries `implementation_type: docs-authoring`. E003 is correctly typed as\n69\tImplementation, not Investigation: it produces artifact changes (reconciled field\n70\tmappings, corrected code, updated fixtures, validation results) rather than resolving a\n71\tquestion that changes downstream structure. No `gated_by` fields are set anywhere, and\n72\tcorrectly so — the open question is resolved by a third-party strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990),\n73\tmodeled per Rule 21 as a tiered-delivery precondition rather than an internal\n74\tInvestigation gate; the summary records this reasoning explicitly. No gating metadata\n75\tissues.\n76\t\n77\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n78\tAll epics are Implementation and carry `ai_signals` (the 9-signal rubric); none carry\n79\t`investigation_signals`. Frontmatter values match the ai-signals rationales in all four\n80\tfiles. Spot checks: E001 `external_dependency: -1` is right (consumes the not-yet-final\n81\texternally-owned metering contract); E003 `open_questions: -1` and `external_dependency:\n82\t-1` are right (the unresolved schema lives there by design); E004 `human_process_gates:\n83\t-1` is right and matches its technical-review AC (Red Hat docs sign-off). Architecture\n84\tcalibration verified against `.context`: E001/E003 `architecture_claims: 1` rationales\n85\tcite `distributed-workloads.md` (Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, Prometheus\n86\tmetrics exposure — confirmed present in the file), E002's cites `dashboard.md` (confirmed),\n87\tand E004's `architecture_claims: 0` is correct because no architecture-context file covers\n88\tthe Documentation component (only dashboard.md and distributed-workloads.md exist).\n89\tComputed `ai_implementability` fields were not checked, per the pipeline-computes rule.\n90\t\n91\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n92\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLRs. E001: correctness verified by\n93\tautomated tests with known inputs, contract tests, CSV-vs-API response equivalence, and\n94\tan explicit no-collection-code AC enforcing the strategy's out-of-scope boundary. E002:\n95\tdisplay, quota-comparison semantics, RBAC scoping, feature-flag toggle, automated UI\n96\tverification. E003: final-schema consumption with no draft-only mappings, E2E validation\n97\tagainst metering source within documented tolerance. E004: the rule-mandated technical\n98\treview AC is present, plus clean publish through the docs pipeline. No replacement or\n99\tkonflux-chain epics exist, so those rule-mandated ACs are not applicable. No soft-AC\n100\tmisfiling: E003's externally-controlled timing (RHAISTRAT-9990 landing) is correctly\n101\trecorded in Risks/Notes rather than as an AC, and its validation ACs condition on what\n102\tthe epic itself verifies. No draft-ID references to sibling epics in any epic body\n103\t(references to RHAISTRAT-9990 are external strategy keys, which are valid).\n104\t\n105\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n106\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: per-project reports over selectable time ranges\n107\t(E001 computation, E002 view), CSV export and stable API for finance tooling (E001),\n108\tcurrent-month vs Kueue quota view (E002, including the admin-scoped access the strategy\n109\timplies), documentation of semantics and export integration (E004). The out-of-scope\n110\tboundaries are respected and enforced (no metering collection code, reports in\n111\tGPU-hours not currency). The strategy's open question and external timing risk are\n112\tcarried forward — Health Warnings 2-3 and the Risks/Not